;
GETTING YOUR RCP/M RUNNING

A - The shared machine
B - First startup
C - Host configuration
:A
THE SHARED MACHINE

HUMONGOUS RCP/M runs CP/M 3 and Z3PLUS under cpmsim. BYE510
looks after the caller connection; AUTH controls caller access.
RBBS provides forums and private mail.

You and the caller share one CP/M computer. The local console is
not a second independent session. Give the caller a chance to finish
before undertaking maintenance.
:B
FIRST STARTUP

Unpack the complete distribution into a writable directory.
Run Start-RCPM.command on macOS, Start-RCPM.sh on Linux or
Start-RCPM.cmd on Windows. Docker has its own startup guide.

The first startup creates a private SYSOP.DOC containing credentials.
Keep it out of the public software collection.

Call your own board using raw TCP at 127.0.0.1, port 4000.
Press RETURN, try DIR SIGM:, MOUNT /L and RBBS, then log off with BYE.
Make a second call to see that the board is ready again.
:C
HOST CONFIGURATION

Stop the system before editing the external RCPM.CONF.
The supplied defaults need no editing.

MODE=direct     Direct TCP (the default)
MODE=ip232      Bundled tcpser virtual modem
ADDRESS         Listener IPv4 address
PORT            Caller port in either mode

Restart with the normal launcher after making changes.
Keep each installation and its writable images separate.
The normal launcher is not a background service. See the separate
host administration guide for unattended operation.
